# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in values. See ENV_SETUP_GUIDE.md for full list.
#
# Firestore: dev defaults to long-polling (avoids Listen/channel 400 on some setups).
# Production: if the console shows firestore.googleapis.com/.../Listen/channel 400, set true and rebuild.
# VITE_FIRESTORE_FORCE_LONG_POLLING=true
# Set to false only if you need to debug the WebChannel transport.
# VITE_FIRESTORE_FORCE_LONG_POLLING=false
#
# --- Local full stack (npm run dev + remote or focused local API) ---
# Proxies browser requests from http://localhost:<vite-port>/api/* to your deployed app (Vite prefers 3000 here).
# If Firebase sign-in fails with auth/requests-from-referer-localhost:5173-are-blocked, add that origin to your
# Google Cloud Browser API key HTTP referrers. See docs/LOCAL_DEV.md.
# Use your Vercel production/preview URL (no trailing slash), or use http://localhost:3001 with `npm run dev:api`.
# DEV_API_PROXY=https://your-app.vercel.app
# DEV_API_PROXY=http://localhost:3001
#
# --- Client API origin (build-time; use when the UI is not served from Vercel) ---
# If you host the SPA on Firebase Hosting or run `vite preview`, relative `/api/*` hits the static host → 404.
# Set to your Vercel app origin (same value as DEV_API_PROXY, no trailing slash). Omit on Vercel.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app
# Omit when echoflux.ai (Vercel) serves both UI and /api. witme.io / *.web.app use echoflux.ai for /api automatically unless overridden here.
#
# Optional: comma-separated extra allowed Origins for browser POSTs to /api (see api/_browserApiCors.ts).
# BROWSER_API_CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-firebase-app.web.app
#
# --- Custom storefront domains (stormijxo.com → / without /handle in path) ---
# Comma-separated; matching ignores leading www. Requires creatorDomains/{host} in Firestore.
# Do NOT list echoflux.ai here — it would route the main app homepage to the fan storefront (stuck loading).
# Code also strips echoflux.ai from this list if misconfigured.
# VITE_CUSTOM_STOREFRONT_HOSTS=stormijxo.com,www.stormijxo.com
#
# --- Stripe (Vercel serverless /api/* — same names in Vercel Project → Settings → Environment Variables) ---
# STRIPE_USE_TEST_MODE=true
# Use ONE of these naming styles for the test secret (code accepts both):
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY_Test=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY_TEST=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY_LIVE=sk_live_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# Optional: Connect-only endpoint signing secret
# STRIPE_CONNECT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# Optional: second Stripe account under the same org (e.g. Stormijxo) — use when that account’s webhook URL
# points to this app’s /api/stripeWebhook so legacy subscriptions still verify and update Firestore.
# STRIPE_STORMIJXO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# Optional: extra whsec_ values, comma-separated (any additional Stripe accounts posting to this endpoint)
# STRIPE_ADDITIONAL_WEBHOOK_SECRETS=whsec_aaa,whsec_bbb
# Creator invite checkout ($1/mo and $2/mo, monthly only; map to recurring Prices in Stripe)
# STRIPE_PRICE_CREATORPRO_MONTHLY=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_CREATORPRO_MONTHLY_Test=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_CREATORPRO_MONTHLY_LIVE=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_CREATORELITE_MONTHLY=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_CREATORELITE_MONTHLY_Test=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_CREATORELITE_MONTHLY_LIVE=price_...
# Success/cancel fallbacks when Origin header is missing
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-domain.com
# Optional: comma-separated creator UIDs that skip Connect (platform-owned storefronts).
# Same list is used for fan-member QA bypass: Witme `users/{uid}.role === "Admin"` OR FAN_PAGE_ADMIN_MEMBER_UIDS
# can open the full member hub on those creators’ pages (see getFanEntitlement + src/lib/fanPageAdminBypass.ts).
# Name must match exactly (or use platform_owner_creators_ids as an alias). Example:
# PLATFORM_OWNER_CREATOR_IDS=yourStormijxoCreatorFirebaseUid
#
# Optional explicit fan UIDs (if not using Firestore Admin role on users/{uid}):
# FAN_PAGE_ADMIN_MEMBER_UIDS=
# Optional extra creators not in PLATFORM_OWNER_CREATOR_IDS:
# FAN_PAGE_ADMIN_MEMBER_CREATOR_IDS=
# FAN_PAGE_ADMIN_MEMBER_HANDLES=stormijxo
#
# --- Rate limiting (production: set both for distributed limits across Vercel instances) ---
# Without these, checkout and other limits fall back to per-instance memory (weaker under load).
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# (Aliases also accepted: KV_REST_API_URL, KV_REST_API_TOKEN)
#
# --- Daily.co platform usage (Admin dashboard — billing cycle resets on the 1st) ---
# Participant-minutes already used this cycle per Daily.co dashboard (before in-app tracking).
# Update DAILY_CO_CYCLE_BASELINE_MONTH when the cycle rolls (e.g. 2026-06 on June 1).
# DAILY_CO_CYCLE_BASELINE_MONTH=2026-05
# DAILY_CO_CYCLE_BASELINE_MINUTES=78
# DAILY_CO_CYCLE_BASELINE_SESSIONS=7
# DAILY_API_KEY=

# --- Vercel Cron (required in Production: set in Vercel → Env; Vercel sends Authorization: Bearer …) ---
# CRON_SECRET=
#
# --- Web push (Fan Hub members) ---
# Firebase Console → Project settings → Cloud Messaging → Web Push certificates → Key pair
# VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=BN...
#
# Dev/staging only: enables legacy no-Stripe entitlement stub at POST /api/purchaseProduct (default off).
# ALLOW_PURCHASE_PRODUCT_STUB=true
